hat the sum of the elements of each row is equal to a constant $ω\\in Γ$ and the sum of the elements of each column is equal to a constant $δ\\in Γ$. In this paper we provide new evidences for the validity of a conjecture proposed by Sylwia Cichacz and Tomasz Hinc on the existence of an $\\mathrm{MRS}_Γ(a,b;c)$.\n# arXiv++ Combinatorics\n\nBrowse math.CO papers from arXiv\n\n## On a conjecture by Sylwia Cichacz and Tomasz Hinc, and a related problem\n\nFiorenza Morini, Marco Antonio Pellegrini, Stefania Sora\n\nPublished: 2024-08-09\n\nNote:\n\nDOI: 10.1016/j.dam.2025.01.040\n\ngroup\n\n# • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\n### Abstract\n\nA $Γ$-magic rectangle set $\\mathrm{MRS}_Γ(a, b; c)$ is a collection of $c$ arrays of size $a\\times b$ whose entries are the elements of an abelian group $Γ$ of order $abc$, each one appearing once and in a unique array in such a way that the sum of the elements of each row is equal to a constant $ω\\in Γ$ and the sum of the elements of each column is equal to a constant $δ\\in Γ$. In this paper we provide new evidences for the validity of a conjecture proposed by Sylwia Cichacz and Tomasz Hinc on the existence of an $\\mathrm{MRS}_Γ(a,b;c)$. We also generalize this problem, describing constructions of $Γ$-magic rectangle sets, whose elements are partially filled arrays.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# SYLWIA CICHĄCZ-PRZENIOSŁO-LIST OF PUBLICATIONS (https://galaxy.agh.edu.pl/~cichacz/cv.pdf)\nciteturn0search18 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 weeks ago; Cichacz, *Irregular graph labelings in Abelian groups*, Ars Mathematica Contemporanea **26**(2) (2026) # P2.09, doi:10.26493/1855-3974.3380.cb8. ... Cichacz, *Partition of Abelian groups into zero-sum sets by complete mappings and its application to the existence of a magic rectangle set*, Journal of Algebraic Combinatorics **61**(24) (2025) doi:10.1007/s10801-025-01392-9.\n---------------------------------------------------------------------